{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Sims 4 adult (human rig) to WoW character skeleton",
  "_about": [
    "Wifecraft's Sims 4 to WoW retarget profile, read by anim/Profile.kt and applied by anim/Retarget.kt.",
    "axes: where each Sims axis goes in WoW model space. Sims 4: y up, a sim faces +z, its left is +x. WoW M2: z up, faces +x, left +y.",
    "bones: sims = the Sims rig bone name (as in the rig, case ignored); wow = the WoW-side name the engine resolves (tools/wow_bones.py, cpp m2.cpp kWowBones);",
    "parent = the mapped WoW bone this one's rotation is local to (WoW bones in between are held at rest while an animation plays);",
    "aim = the mapped WoW bone it points at, for the rest-pose conversion (wowRest); flip = rotation axis components to negate (x, y, z; a last-resort fix);",
    "position = the bone's movement is applied too (the root alone).",
    "drop: Sims bones never mapped (slots, IK targets and poles, twist and CAS slider bones, face rig, props), as globs. Unmapped bones still move their children.",
    "wowRest and rootHeight: written by python3 -I wifecraft/tools/wow_bones.py --profile THIS_FILE DIR 921844 (night elf female's pivots). Rerun it after changing an aim.",
    "Bone names: the Sims 4 human rig's, from the community's rig documentation; unverified against a rig from the game until a player's skeleton is loaded."
  ],
  "axes": {"x": "+y", "y": "+z", "z": "+x"},
  "positionScale": 1.2,
  "trackSpace": "absolute",
  "bones": [
